\date{2026-10-31T04:30:12Z}
\title{Monomorphism}
\taxon{Definition}
\author{hsuchingchung}
\import{macros-subobj}

\p{

A morphism #{f : A \r B} in a category \CCat is called a \strong{monomorphism} if

##{ f g = f h \text{ implies } g = h }

for all morphisms #{g, h: C \r A}. 
}

\p{In this case, we also write #{f : A \hookrightarrow B} or say #{f} is \strong{monic}.}